WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.259 --> 00:00:01.133
- Christ.

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.839
(swooshing)

00:00:02.839 --> 00:00:04.084
(squeaky hinges)

00:00:04.084 --> 00:00:08.731
(rock music)

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:15.252
- This is considered
the traditional staple

00:00:15.252 --> 00:00:16.738
for most people most mornings.

00:00:16.738 --> 00:00:17.651
(laughs)

00:00:17.651 --> 00:00:21.102
We have the fried bread, English bacon,

00:00:21.102 --> 00:00:22.788
which is English back bacon.

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:25.856
It's obviously a different
taste to the American bacon.

00:00:25.856 --> 00:00:27.522
The pork sausage, which we have

00:00:27.522 --> 00:00:29.871
made with our British butcher.

00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:32.959
Um, Heinz baked beans, which are imported,

00:00:32.959 --> 00:00:35.540
um, baked beans from England.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.668
Fried tomatoes, grilled tomatoes here.

00:00:38.668 --> 00:00:41.615
Then, underneath, we've
got fried mushrooms.

00:00:41.615 --> 00:00:46.328
The black pudding, which is
also known as blood pudding.

00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:47.669
Where I'm from, the West Midlands,

00:00:47.669 --> 00:00:49.390
it's known as a delicacy.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.354
- Ooh.

00:00:51.354 --> 00:00:53.294
I think American bacon is better.

00:00:53.294 --> 00:00:54.780
It's greasier, I mean
if you're going to get

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.685
something unhealthy, just,
like, go all the way, you know?

00:00:57.685 --> 00:00:59.879
- This is really good,
it's really hearty, but...

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:02.094
I think ours is just a little bit better.

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:04.486
- This looks more like a hotdog.

00:01:04.486 --> 00:01:06.315
- Mmmm.

00:01:06.315 --> 00:01:07.295
- What my tastebuds are telling me

00:01:07.295 --> 00:01:08.867
is that this is deep fried in butter,

00:01:09.677 --> 00:01:12.593
and, um, it's fantastic.

00:01:13.453 --> 00:01:16.401
- Mmm, oh my God.

00:01:16.401 --> 00:01:17.790
- Who makes better toast?

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:18.704
England.

00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:19.932
- I feel like it's so random to have

00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:21.923
just a plain tomato for breakfast.

00:01:21.923 --> 00:01:23.772
- While I'm not a big fan of tomatoes,

00:01:23.772 --> 00:01:25.683
I can appreciate a tomato, and this is

00:01:25.683 --> 00:01:26.954
a really, really good one.

00:01:26.954 --> 00:01:28.153
- Mushrooms, they're ok.

00:01:28.153 --> 00:01:29.656
I feel like these belong in an omelette.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:32.033
On their own, uh, they seem lonely.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:33.335
- [Woman] Are beans a vegetable?

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:34.603
- Also, beans...

00:01:34.603 --> 00:01:36.803
Not a breakfast food in America.

00:01:36.803 --> 00:01:38.189
- You know what, if I could have

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:40.120
the sauce of the beans, that's good.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.436
- English breakfast is
basically like a barbeque.

00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:44.813
- Black pudding is made of blood?

00:01:44.813 --> 00:01:45.971
Lovely.

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:47.799
- It kind of looks like, uh...

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:48.937
corned beef hash.

00:01:48.937 --> 00:01:50.847
- It's got, like, little nuggets in there.

00:01:50.847 --> 00:01:51.761
I don't know what those are.

00:01:51.761 --> 00:01:53.509
- I'm not a big fan of it on its own.

00:01:53.509 --> 00:01:55.784
- Pudding is chocolate,

00:01:55.784 --> 00:01:57.430
and dessert and sweet.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.976
You told me I'm going
to have black pudding!

00:02:01.629 --> 00:02:02.726
- Listen, I mean this has been

00:02:02.726 --> 00:02:03.925
a very interesting experience,

00:02:03.925 --> 00:02:05.977
but, to be honest, I still think that

00:02:05.977 --> 00:02:07.846
the American breakfast is the strong one.

00:02:07.846 --> 00:02:08.943
- English breakfast is better than

00:02:08.943 --> 00:02:10.400
American breakfast, I'm sorry.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.530
- This or Cinnamon Toast Crunch?

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.592
I think this wins.

00:02:14.592 --> 00:02:16.664
- Gotta give it to America,

00:02:16.664 --> 00:02:20.240
cause, America, you can
have dessert for breakfast,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.048
you can have, you know, like you can have

00:02:22.048 --> 00:02:23.938
something sweet, you can
have something savory.

00:02:23.938 --> 00:02:25.990
This just feels like dinner.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:28.895
So it's a tie?

00:02:28.895 --> 00:02:29.729
I think we might have just started

00:02:29.729 --> 00:02:31.880
a second Revolutionary War.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.213
(rock music)

00:02:36.213 --> 00:02:37.541
(swooshing)

00:02:37.541 --> 00:02:38.941
(squeaky hinges)

